  "machines": 2,
  "setup": "Head (rank 0, API) + worker (rank 1, --headless, same args with NODE_RANK=1) containers over the CX7 RoCE fabric (--nnodes 2, mp executor). Set NODE_RANK, HEAD_IP, NODE_IP, CX7_IF and CX7_IB on each node; NODE_IP must be its reachable fabric IP. Both nodes download the pinned 0xSero/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-Spark repository to local NVMe and mount it at /model. This public repository includes the native checkpoint, Engram parts and EXL3 banks; no separate full upstream checkpoint is needed. After download, run bash ~/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-Spark-08ac8b3d/reassemble.sh once on each node to reconstruct and sha256-check the two Engram shards. Allow about 665 GB for download plus reassembly, in addition to image/cache space; after a successful check the .partNN files may be deleted, leaving about 462 GB. The plan is /model/exl3/plan/J268-ho-v31-K5n.json; its qdir is qn:q31:q31s relative to --workdir /model/exl3. Mount a persistent /cache for b12x and RoCE JIT caches. The source repository includes a host memory guard to stop containers before a GB10 unified-memory OOM. Load about 12 minutes. CANDIDATE: the earlier S018 lab run used the original local full-checkpoint layout and the unattested host image; the final published layout and approved CI image still require a fresh six-gate run.",
